    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\"> The Jaguaress, an eccentric Andean deity, greets you at the velvet curtain and casts you as Inti, a young man who dreamed of being a drug lord but landed in prison. Prison X is an immersive mythological play sweeping you into a Bolivian prison, where you coexist with devils and corrupt prison guards.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Festivals where Prison X premiered: Sundance Film Festival, Cannes XR, SXSW and Games for Change in New York.\u00a0  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\"> The Jaguaress, an eccentric Andean deity, greets you at the velvet curtain and casts you as Inti, a young man who dreamed of being a drug lord but landed in prison. Prison X is an immersive mythological play sweeping you into a Bolivian prison, where you coexist with devils and corrupt prison guards.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Festivals where Prison X premiered: Sundance Film Festival, Cannes XR, SXSW and Games for Change in New York.\u00a0  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p>",
    "short_description": "Heavy doors open and you're swept into the surreal world of Prison X, an infamous Bolivian jail in the Neo-Andean underworld. As you navigate amongst devils, saints, wicked characters, corrupt prison guards and even a Western filmmaker; hold onto your soul so La Diabla doesn't snatch it away.",
    "supported_languages": "English<strong>*</strong><br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support",
    "reviews": "\u201cThe Best Non-Linear Narrative... The most ambitious interactive narrative piece this year (2021)\u201d<br>Voices of VR<br><br>\u201cCaptured a state of dream logic that I so often want in VR\u201d<br>Jesse Damiani - Forbes<br><br>\u201cAsserts Indigenous aesthetics and cosmologies that not only were erased and devalued by colonial Spanish rule but are woefully underrepresented in digital media today\u201d<br>Art in America<br>",
